From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tom Englund <tomenglund26@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 23:36:59 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] nvidia-drm: only send the HDCP topology uevent when the
 topology changes

RM posts an HDCP status change (disabled/inactive) on every DPMS off.
nvkms turns that into a CP_TOPOLOGY_CHANGED event with a cleared
topology, and nv_drm_connector_update_topology_property() replaced the
blob and sent a HOTPLUG=1 connector property uevent each time, even
when the topology was already clear. Compositors answer every hotplug
uevent by force-probing all connectors.

It also did this for connectors that never got the content protection
properties (only DP and HDMI do), which trips the WARN_ON in
drm_sysfs_connector_property_event() on DVI.

Skip connectors without the properties, and skip the update when the
topology is unchanged (a missing blob counts as an all-zero topology).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-connector.c | 19 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 19 insertions(+)

diff --git a/kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-connector.c b/kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-connector.c
index 79407636..335b1161 100644
--- a/kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-connector.c
+++ b/kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-connector.c
@@ -999,8 +999,27 @@ int nv_drm_connector_update_topology_property(struct nv_drm_connector *nv_connec
     struct nv_drm_connector_state *nv_state = to_nv_drm_connector_state(state);
     struct drm_device *dev = connector->dev;
     struct nv_drm_device *nv_dev = to_nv_device(dev);
+    const struct drm_property_blob *old_blob = nv_state->hdcp_topology_blob;
     int ret;
 
+    /* The content protection properties are only attached to DP and HDMI */
+    if ((nv_connector->type != NVKMS_CONNECTOR_TYPE_DP) &&
+        (nv_connector->type != NVKMS_CONNECTOR_TYPE_HDMI)) {
+        return 0;
+    }
+
+    /*
+     * RM reports HDCP disabled/inactive on every DPMS off, which clears an
+     * already clear topology.  Don't send a hotplug uevent for that: it makes
+     * compositors force-probe every connector.
+     */
+    if ((old_blob != NULL) ?
+        ((old_blob->length == NVKMS_HDCP_TOPOLOGY_SIZE) &&
+         (memcmp(old_blob->data, topology, NVKMS_HDCP_TOPOLOGY_SIZE) == 0)) :
+        (memchr_inv(topology, 0, NVKMS_HDCP_TOPOLOGY_SIZE) == NULL)) {
+        return 0;
+    }
+
     ret = drm_property_replace_global_blob(dev,
                                             &nv_state->hdcp_topology_blob,
                                             NVKMS_HDCP_TOPOLOGY_SIZE,
